      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-12-21_WidnesExaminer_art0163" n="art0163">
        <head>Examiner, Saturday, December 21, 1912.</head>
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, December 21, 1912.</p>
        <p>INSURANCE BABIES. MR. A. H. GROSFIELD.S INTERESTING</p>
        <p>OFFER.</p>
        <p>The benefits of the National Insurance Act will come into operation on January 15th and Mr. A. H. Crosfield has decided to mark the occasion in an interesting and practical manner. To the child of any insured worker in the borough, which is born between 12 o'clock midnight on January 14th and 12 o'clock midnight on January 15th, Mr. Cros- field will present a silver spoon, with the child's name engraved thereon. The parents will also receive a large photograph of them- selves and the child. The offer is open to all insured workers, irrespective of party.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-12-21_WidnesExaminer_art0164" n="art0164">
        <head>TERRITORIAL PRIZE DISTRIBUTION.</head>
        <p>TERRITORIAL PRIZE DISTRIBUTION.</p>
        <p>"A PETTY-FOGGING CONTROVERSY."</p>
        <p>Last evening the annual prize distribution in c n- nection with the 4th Battalion Prince of Wales Volunteers, South Lancashire Regt., was held in the , Drill Ball. The proceedings took the form of hot-pot Isupper and smoking concert. During an interval the prizes were tistributed by Col. J Reid Walker. In reviewing the year's work Col. Brereton Fair- Clough said the strength of the battalion was 020, an increase of 10. Alluding to the recert speeches by Lord Roberts and others on the efficiency of the force he said he hoped the territorials and the public were above being affected by "this petty-fogging con- troversy." PRIZE LIST. Winners of Battalion Wield (presented by Colonel McCarthy O'Leary). G Company. Cap:ain P N Avery. Winners of silver bowl (presented by General F Roome, C.B ), E Company, Captain H Owen. (lifters cup (revolver competition), Ist Captain and Adjutant 0 Elgood. Officers cup and box of cigars, Ist Lieut Colonel B Fairclough. Box of cigarettes 2nd Lieut and Quarter-Master 0 H Ingram, E Company. Solano target competition, lat Colour-Sergeant T Boardmans team, ; 2nd C Company, Sergeant T Bosswards team, £3; 3rd D Company, Sorg cant H Whitflelds team, £2. Permanent staff competition, Ist Sergeant Major M Newell, £1 Ios. ; 2nd Sergeant Instructor EHacket, 10s.</p>
        <p>• WINNERS OF COMPANY CUPS. A Company (for General Efficiency) presented by Colonel J D Buckton, Lance-Corporal F E Callaghan ; B Company (for shooting) presented by Mr W ocaen. Lance-Corporal .1 Miosbull ; D Company (for shooting) presented by Mr J H Ede!sten, Lance-Corporal J Stout; F Company (for general efficiency) presented by Mr II Roberts, Sergeant E W Sankey ' • F Company (for shooting) presented by Mr W Dimelow; Private A Mather ; D Company (for Recruits) presented by Mr W II Hinckley, Recruit C Martin ,• F Company (for Recruits) presented by Captain Gooch, Recruit A B SLaw. BEST SHOT IN COMPANIES IN THE ANNUAL COURSE, IST, 15s ; 2nd, 103 :—A Company, 1, Colour-Sergeant J Allardice ; 2. Lance Corporal Callaghan ; B Company. 1, Lance-Corporal 3 Minshull 2. Pricate 3 W Longnion.e '•'(...1 Company, 1, Sergeant T Bostrr-ard ; 2, Private THalley ; 1) Company. 1, Lance-Corporal 3 Stout ; 2, Sergi. ro.t A Wood ; E Company, 1, Colour. Sergeant T Boardman ; 2, Corporal W Knowles ; F Company, 1, Private A Mather; 2, Private J alnakett ; G Company, 1, Private J Wilson ; 20Sergeant A E Lewis ; H Company, 1, Sergeant D Ridyard ; 2, Private R. Littlewood. REC RUITS' COM P ETIT 1074.—Private S Woodall, C Company, 30s ; Private J Crookes, D Company, 20.3 ; Private .1 Boller, C Company, 15s ; Private G Green, E Company, Os • Lance-Corporal H Goodwin,B Company, 10-1 ; Private h Smith, H Company, 10s : Private G Littler, E Company, lOs ; Privato H Stead, E Company, lOs Private W Dwerryhouse,H Company, 10a ; Private P Rooney, E Company, lOs ; Privates B Carhis, E Corn pany, C Roberts, C Company, J Walker, G Company, T Burns, E Company, G Ashton, F Company, G Jackson, E Company. W A Brown, A Company, G Sumner, H Company, B Tully, E Company, H Hamblett, E Com- pany, H B Hardman, E Company, E Marsden, E Company, .1 Hind, D Company, P Lucas, J Lightfoot, A Company, H Rowley, A Company, J Roberts, E Company, H Barker, B Company, H Daniels H Company, A Breeze A Company, T Littler G Company, T Collins F Company. J Middleham G Company. E Preece D Company, .1 Flemming H Com- pany, II Wood D Company, W Sollery C Company, .1 Brockley E Company,sl O'Hara E Company,J Dimelow, , E Company, J Buttery A Company, A Boardman E Company. 2s 60 each. BEST SHOT COMPETITION.—COIoUr-Serat 3 Allardice, A Company, £4 ; Sergeant T Smith, H Company, .£3 ; Sergeant A Wood,D Company, £2 ; Private J Thornton, H Company. Li: Sergeant C Libbitter, A Company, £.l; Private A Ball, E Company, 21 •, W' Newne,F Company, 106 • Corporal T Edwards, Company, lOs; Private A liodpson., A Company, les ; Sergeant W Newport, E Company, 10s. BATTALION COMPETITION.—Private H W Eckersley, 0 Company. £2; Sergeant E Dower, F Company, Sergeant H Whitfield, D Company, Private Et Smith, H Company, Lance-Corporal R Littlewood, H Company, £1 each ; Private G Cliffs, A Company, Colour. Sergeant T roardman, E Company, Sergeant Dr T Clarke, H Company, Sergeant A E Lewis, 0 Company, Sergeant T Gill, F Company, Sergeant G Sutton, E Company, Corporal II U Dudley, G Company, Private S T Ince, A Company, Private B Ken urrigh t, C Com- pany, Private H Ellam, E Company, 15s each ; Corporal A Allcork, H Company, Recruit A Breeze, A Company, Private W H Potter, H Company, Private G Heath, A j Company, Col.-Sergeant C Walker, C Company, Private 3 Naylor, E Company, Sergeant T Bossward, C Company, Private J D Hoywortb, G Company, Lance Corporal D Dewar C Company, Private H Burland, B Company, 10s each ; Privates J Longworth,F Company,E Melling, A Company, A E Tew, G Company. H Fletcher, Com- pany, Sergeant T Shovelton, A Company, Privates 1' Harrop, A Company, .1 Roberta, E Company, C Pilling, C Company, Lance-Corporal J Stout. Colour-Sergeant H S Morris, D Company, Sergeant H Jeffs, G Company, Privates J Raspin, A Company, 3 Butler, C Company, J W Hinds, A Company, Lance-Corporal V Derbyshire, G Company, 5s each ; Sergeant D Ridyard,H Company, Privates E Weaver, B Company, J W Marsh, H Com- pany, C Cliffs, A Company, F Halley. F Company, Fl Hough, H Company, Sergeant R Rigby, D Com- pany. Privates A Aabton, A Company, A Houghton, A Company, J S Pritchard, A Company, J Tole, C Company, Recruit R Hill, 0 Company, Privates P Heaney, A Company, H Bedworth, E Company, G M Crooke', B Company, J Burns, E Company, J Hamnett, E Company, F Hogg, F Company, S Pierce, G Company, F Houghton, B Company, 2s 6d each. _ _</p>
        <p>'7—S-1-GNAWING PRlZES.—SArgesnt J Betts (Instruoto-s Certificate), £3: Corporal 3 Slevin (Lnstrnotors Certifi- cate), £2 •, Privates 3D Heyworth, £2 ss; G Lomas, %V Herding, gi 5s ; T Carbis, 21 15s: H Braddock, M Lomas, P Smith, £1 53; Corporal S Hamblett, .C 1 15s ; Privates A J Bray, A S.nders, B Carbis, £1 Sc; 0 Potts, 15s ; Lance-Corporals F R NicCollum, £1 15s; C J Sheath, £l. Ss ; Privates P N Owen, W H Potter, 15s ; F Atherton, 21 5s ; A Lomas, Lance-Corporal D Dewar, Lance-Sergeant W Ness, Lance-Corporal V Derbyshire, 158 ' • Privates J Litherland, G M Crookes, M Forster, F Middlebam, T Littler, ss.</p>
        <p>KING GEORGE AND HIS BIBLE. The King, through Lord Knoll, has sent the following letter to Mr F C Brawling, secretary of the Scripture Gift Mission:— Dear Sir.—l have had the bononr of submitting your letter to the King, and I am directed to inform you in reply that it is quite true that he promised Queen Alexandra, as long ago as 1881, that he would read a chapter of the Bible daily, and that he has ever since adhered to this promise.—Yours very truly, ENOLLYS.</p>
