        <head>ISINESS HMS 9 to 8 DAILY.</head>
        <p>ISINESS HMS 9 to 8 DAILY.</p>
        <p>services of the ever-popular Mr Wallington as head- master. (Applause.) Peoplo's College had long been in the forefront of education in Warrington and he submitted that it still retained that position. (Applause.) In proof of that statement he would mention that out of six scholarships at the Boteler Grammar School offered during the past year, no fewer than five were obtained by pupils of People's College. (Applause.) Since the opening of the Municipal Secondary School, 200 scholars from People's College bad suece,sfully passed the entrance examination—a very creditable proportion of the total. (Applause.)</p>
