        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. CHESHIRE INSURANCE COMMITTEE.— MEDICAL BENEFIT. SUPPLY OF DRUGS AND APPLIANCES. NOTICE is hereby given that all Chemists and others who may be desirous of undertaking the Supply of DRUGS and APPLIANCES to Insured Persons resident in the Committee's area are requested to at once apply to me the undersigned for particulars of conditions and forms of contract under which the supply may be undertaken. FRANK T. WEST, County Insurance Offices, Clerk to the Committee. 100;Northgate et , Chester. --COUNTY PALATI NE 75-07.3t1ESTtiat. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will be holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 30th day of December, 1912, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of 13roxton, Chester Castle, Daresbury, Eddisbury, Nantwich, Runcorn, Winsford, and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Divisions, will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester' at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 30th day of December, 1912, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, on WEDNESDAY, the IsT DAY OF JANUARY, 1913, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincharn, Bucklow,Dukinfield, Middlewich, Sandbach, Congletoo,Northwich, Presthury and Stockport, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford at the opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the is day of January, 1913, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 17th December, 1912.</p>
